# HOWTO test xds decoder
  The testxds.c sets up the xds decoder,
  In userdata(708) mode, the 708 decoder will be set up, the decoder will sort the userdata packets, extract and relay the 608 data to internal 608 decoder.
  In vbi(608) mode, the 608 decoder will be set up to run the decoding.

  The vbi data and userdata will be got from the ccdataserver runs on the platform.

  Setup steps:
  1. data source:
  Run the ccdataserver on the platform

  2. test:
  2.1 test userdata
  ```bash
  testxds
  ```
  2.2 test vbi
  ```bash
  # ln -s testxds testxds.vbi
  # testxds.vbi
  ```

  Note: the xds test can run remotely on a PC, which gets data through ip socket, as the dataserver supports ip distribution.
  ```bash
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH="./build:../ccdataserver/build" ./build/testxds <ccdataserver ip> <ccdataserver port>
  ```


# HOWTO test xds 608 decoder individually
   The test608.c sets up the xds 608 decoder,
   reads the 608 data from STDIN as input to feed the xds decoder.

   On PC, raw 608 data can be got from ccextractor's RCWT output.
   rcwt_dump.c is the RCWT adaptor, acts as a server.
   The ccextractor implements an output method which communicates with the server and send the cc raw data to server.
   The protocol is a bit complicated, rcwt_dump.c will handle the protocol and dump the cc data to the STDOUT.

   Setup steps:
   1. test:
   ```bash
   ./build/rcwt_dump 33333 | LD_LIBRARY_PATH="./build:../ccdataserver/build" ./build/test608
   ```

   2. data source: 
   ```bash
   tsp -I file -i atsc.ts -P regulate -b 20000000 | ccextractor --stdin --cbraw --program-number 1 --fullbin --sendto localhost:33333
   ```

